--- a/docs/content/archive.md
+++ b/docs/content/archive.md
@@ -100,6 +100,30 @@ kacak/
 ```
 
 
+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are skipped by default. Use
+`-l/--links` to expose them as regular files with a `.rclonelink`
+suffix holding the link target, in the same way as the local backend.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+```
+
+Copying with `--links` to a destination which supports them recreates
+the symbolic links:
+
+```
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular archive member whose name ends in `.rclonelink` is not
+affected - it stays a regular file.
+
 ## Modification times
 
 Modification times are preserved with an accuracy depending on the archive type.
